### Nested Schema for `boot_disk`

The boot disk is created before the VM is powered on. The provider adopts an existing drive with the same name instead of creating a second disk. Removing `boot_disk` deletes that one drive and leaves every other drive on the VM alone. Changing `media` or `source` replaces the VM.

Optional:

- `name` (String) - Drive name. Defaults to `boot`. Set this to the existing drive name when a single-disk VM moves off the old `vergeio_drive` block.
- `size` (Number) - Size in GB (supports fractional values, e.g., 8.5).
- `source` (Number) - Media source id for a clone or import. Changing source replaces the VM.
- `media` (String) - Media type. Omit it for a new disk. Changing media replaces the VM.
	- `cdrom`   (CD-Rom)
	- `disk`    (New Disk)
	- `import`  (Import drive from media images)
	- `clone`   (Clone an existing VM disk)
	- `efidisk` (Create a new EFI Disk)
	- `nonpersistent` (Non-persistent disk)

Read-Only:

- `key` (String) - Drive key assigned by VergeOS.

